The dialogue box's button frames (SYSTEM_W, u 0x4C v 0xB7) tell the base: the US disc's 6x5 × (0xC/0xD) or the
Japanese disc's 8x5 ○ (7/0xE/0xF). modButtonsBoot reads SYSTEM_W.TIM at boot, before the saves' options
(modBootOptions), and a Japanese ○ turns the option on; a save's options still win. With the Japanese ○, ON keeps
the disc's own ○ and OFF shows ours: the ellipse painted over with the face and a 6x5 × in the blue of the
PlayStation's × (112,176,248)/(64,96,208), in a CLUT of our own in the page's filler (as the US disc's red ○ ring).
The US disc is unchanged. One executable for every base. 464 bytes of heap.
